@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "employee.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki to OSB Employee Integration
	Testing employee sync updates in OSB caused by changes in Koroneiki.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View Liferay employee
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	New Liferay employees who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - DXP"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Portal"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Commerce"

Scenario: Remove Liferay employee
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	New Liferay employees who are removed from the Liferay Inc org on okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I remove the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" from the okta group "Employees"
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should not be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - DXP"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Portal"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Commerce"

Scenario: Remove Liferay employee and login via okta
	New Liferay employees who are removed from the Liferay Inc org on okta and login via okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I remove the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" from the okta group "Employees"
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should not be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - DXP"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Portal"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Commerce"

Scenario: View Liferay Data Access US employee
	New Liferay employees who are members of Data Access US who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I assign the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the okta group "Data Access US"
	Then the team with the name "Account Access US" should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Data Access US"

Scenario: View Liferay Data Access EU employee
	New Liferay employees who are members of Data Access EU who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I assign the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the okta group "Data Access EU"
	Then the team with the name "Account Access EU" should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Data Access EU"

Scenario: Resync removed Liferay employee from customer organizations
	New Liferay employees who are added to koroneiki via okta should resync correctly to OSB if removed from their groups.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I unset the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" from the support organization "Employees"
	And I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"

Scenario: Resync deleted Liferay employee from customer
	New Liferay employees who are deleted from customer should resync correctly to OSB if an okta login is performed.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I delete the user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" from customer.liferay.com
	And I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"

Scenario: View Liferay Subscription Services employee
	Employees members of the Division Subscription Services group should be added to Division Subscription Services organization

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	| Group         | Division - Subscription Services |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	And the team with the name "Systems - Provisioning" should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Employees"
	And the user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Division - Subscription Services"
	And I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Division - Subscription Services"

Scenario: View Liferay CS Data Access US employee
	New Liferay employees who are members of CS Data Access US okta group who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I assign the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the okta group "CS - Data Access US"
	Then the team with the name "Account Access US" should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Data Access US"

